00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:19.220
- I have a small problem
with the way the doctor

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:20.970
presented all the options to the patient.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.900
And while it's important
to give the patient

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.490
all the possibilities and all the options,

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:27.830
I think right here we're
jumping to a lot of conclusions.

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:29.290
The way that I would do this is in order.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:31.510
First, I would tell the
patient what we know.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.160
We see a tumor on the CAT scan.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.080
Now we've done the MRI and
we've in fact confirmed

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.460
that there is a tumor present.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:39.330
We then have to say that in
order to confirm what kind

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:41.110
of tumor and the staging of the tumor

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.800
we would have to perform a biopsy.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:44.020
We would then give options

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:45.640
of all the things that could happen

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:49.370
depending on whether or not
the tumor is a certain grade.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:51.730
We wouldn't go into these
details, we will just say,

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.900
depending on what we find
you may need chemotherapy,

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.830
radiation or perhaps even surgery.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.520
Now here's the most important step.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:01.910
If a patient is against radiation,
chemotherapy and surgery,

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:04.130
you do not perform the biopsy.

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:06.320
The purpose of performing the biopsy

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.710
is to act on the results.

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:09.543
And if you already know

00:04:09.543 --> 00:04:11.300
that you're not gonna act on the results

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.920
the biopsy is just putting
the patient at a high risk

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.740
for complications without
any benefit being added.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:18.670
A great example of this is I had a patient

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:20.450
who is in her late 80s,

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:22.550
who we suspected to have colon cancer.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:25.580
And as a result, we recommended
her getting a colonoscopy

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.560
so that we can then treat the cancer

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.000
and get it surgically removed.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.190
She said, very clearly,
I will never want surgery

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:33.710
at this point in my life.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.510
I am happy with the way my life is,

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:36.620
and I've lived long enough,

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:39.930
and that is my patient
autonomy being spoken, fine.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.460
Then we shouldn't even do the colonoscopy

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.360
in the first place,
because if the colonoscopy

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:45.050
is just gonna tell us that
there's a cancer there,

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.140
but the patient already knows

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.430
that they don't want to act on it.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:50.240
Save the test, save the
patient to discomfort.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:52.050
Allow them to have a good quality of life,

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:53.250
and that's what should be done here.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.100
Now, it's also important to note

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.730
that even if you know
removing a part of a tumor

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.250
might not improve a
patient's survivability,

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:03.500
meaning it doesn't extend
their five-year survival rate,

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:04.333
for example.

00:05:04.333 --> 00:05:05.830
But we know that during those five years

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:08.590
if we shrink the size of
the tumor with the surgery

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:10.400
we can at least give them
a better quality of life.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.760
For example, they get less headaches.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.740
It might be worthwhile to
proceed with that surgery.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:16.430
That is why we give all
these options to patients

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:18.190
and get a really good understanding

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:19.310
of what their symptoms are,

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:22.107
before we jump in to
give our recommendations.

